    "In edge layouts, every mirror-unrecoverable cell (y,x) has x<=1 and 14<=y<=17 (or the transposed condition y<=1 and 14<=x<=17), and its transpose partner (x,y) is visible. A 13x13 window around such a cell then lies entirely in off-diagonal block territory, where the plain transpose is consistent.",
    "Output always differs from the input region because it replaces 8s with pattern colours."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "All original grids are 30x30. Smaller sizes extrapolate the mechanism and are not claimed as observed native task sizes.",
    "Quadrant content is uniformly random within the block-symmetry constraints, so it lacks the smaller hand-designed motifs of the original patterns.",
    "Edge-layout support is restricted to the region where the plain transpose is locally consistent; masks needing diagonal-block anti-transpose recovery are not generated.",
    "Fixture quadrants are stored explicitly as latent data. The test quadrant's six masked cells (rows 14-15, cols 0-2) are taken from the canonical output, which agrees with the block transpose."
  ],
